class SummaryRanges {
    private Map&lt;Integer, Node&gt; map;
    private UnionFind uf;
    public SummaryRanges() {
        this.map = new HashMap&lt;&gt;();   
        this.uf = new UnionFind();
    }

    public void addNum(int value) {
        if (map.containsKey(value)) return;

        Node node = new Node(value);
        map.put(value, node);
        if (map.containsKey(value - 1)) {
            uf.union(node, map.get(value - 1));
        }

        if (map.containsKey(value + 1)) {
            uf.union(node, map.get(value + 1));
        }
    }

    public int[][] getIntervals() {
        Set&lt;Node&gt; nodes = new HashSet&lt;&gt;();
        for (Node node : map.values()) {
            Node root = uf.find(node);
            nodes.add(root);
        }

        List&lt;Node&gt; sortedNodes = new ArrayList&lt;&gt;(nodes);
        sortedNodes.sort((a, b) -&gt; Integer.compare(a.min, b.min));
        int[][] res = new int[sortedNodes.size()][2];
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; sortedNodes.size(); i++) {
            res[i][0] = sortedNodes.get(i).min;
            res[i][1] = sortedNodes.get(i).max;
        }
        return res;

    }

    public class Node {
        public int value;
        public Node parent;
        public int rank;
        public int min;
        public int max;

        public Node(int value) {
            this.value = value;
            this.parent = this;
            this.rank = 0;
            this.min = value;
            this.max = value;
        }
    }

    public class UnionFind {
        public void union(Node x, Node y) {
            Node rx = find(x);
            Node ry = find(y);
            if (rx == ry) return;

            if (rx.rank &gt; ry.rank) {
                ry.parent = rx;
                rx.min = Math.min(rx.min, ry.min);
                rx.max = Math.max(rx.max, ry.max);
            } else if (rx.rank &lt; ry.rank) {
                rx.parent = ry;
                ry.min = Math.min(ry.min, rx.min);
                ry.max = Math.max(ry.max, rx.max);
            } else {
                ry.parent = rx;
                rx.rank++;
                rx.min = Math.min(rx.min, ry.min);
                rx.max = Math.max(rx.max, ry.max);
            }
        }

        public Node find(Node node) {
            while (node != node.parent) {
                node = node.parent;
            }
            return node;
        }
    }
}

Union Find
This is a very interesting union find application.
To apply union find, we first define the Node class to represent a variable. One key element in the class is the weight attribute which denotes the weight from the current node to its parent node. For example, with the equation a / b = 2.0, we could define node a and b correspondingly, and set a.parent = b and a.weight = 2.0.
The UnionFind class defines the two key operations: union(Node x, Node y, double value) and find(Node node).

union(): this function connects two nodes together.
find(): this function not only looks up the root node of the given node, but also compresses the path along the path.

Within the union() function, it might not be obvious why we have rx.weight = value * y.weight / x.weight. To derive this, consider the following scenario:

a / b = 2.0
c / d = 2.0

Now we have a.parent = b and a.weight = 2.0. In addition, we have c.parent = d and c.weight = 2.0.
Suppose we have another euqation a / c = 3.0 and we need to call union(c, d, 3.0). Realize that:

a = a.weight * b
c = c.weight * d

Now we have \(\frac{c}{d} = \frac{a.weight \times b}{c.weight \times d} = 3.0\). Then we can have b / d = 3.0 * c.weight / a.weight, which is the formula used in the union() function.
Note that we are seprating the union find data structure from the algorithm operating on it. Specifically, we use a map to hold all the nodes that represent all the variables given in the equations. The UnionFind class defines the operations on the map.
class Solution {
    public double[] calcEquation(List&lt;List&lt;String&gt;&gt; equations, double[] values, List&lt;List&lt;String&gt;&gt; queries) {
        Map&lt;String, Node&gt; map = new HashMap&lt;&gt;();
        UnionFind uf = new UnionFind();
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; equations.size(); i++) {
            List&lt;String&gt; lst = equations.get(i);
            String a = lst.get(0);
            String b = lst.get(1);
            double value = values[i];

            if (!map.containsKey(a)) {
                map.put(a, new Node());
            }
            if (!map.containsKey(b)) {
                map.put(b, new Node());
            }

            uf.union(map.get(a), map.get(b), value);
        }

        double[] res = new double[queries.size()];
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; queries.size(); i++) {
            List&lt;String&gt; lst = queries.get(i);
            String a = lst.get(0), b = lst.get(1);
            if (map.containsKey(a) && map.containsKey(b) && uf.find(map.get(a)) == uf.find(map.get(b))) {
                res[i] = map.get(a).weight / map.get(b).weight;
            } else {
                res[i] = -1;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    public class Node {
        public Node parent;
        public double weight;

        public Node() {
            this.parent = this;
            this.weight = 1.0;
        }
    }

    public class UnionFind {
        public void union(Node x, Node y, double value) {
            Node rx = find(x);
            Node ry = find(y);
            if (rx == ry) return;

            rx.parent = ry;
            rx.weight = value * y.weight / x.weight;
        }

        public Node find(Node node) {
            Node temp = node;
            double weight = 1.0;
            while (temp != temp.parent) {
                weight *= temp.weight;
                temp = temp.parent;
            }
            node.parent = temp;
            node.weight = weight;
            return node.parent;
        }
    }
}

